<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}_{x}\big(\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}_{x}\big(\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⩽</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex129.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>err</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In that case, since the total sum is less than <math id="A7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>err</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that each term must be less than <math id="A7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>err</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the lemma holds.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 12</span></span><span id="Thmlemma12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{x,y,t}|A_{t}(x,y)|\leqslant A\in\mathbb{R}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{x,y,t}|A_{t}(x,y)|\leqslant A\in\mathbb{R}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform over <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then with <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\sqrt{\ln(|\mathcal{Y}|)/(A^{2}T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\sqrt{\ln(|\mathcal{Y}|)/(A^{2}T)}</annotation></semantics></math>, for the sequence of policies computed by REBEL, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma12.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\forall\pi,x:\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}A_{t}(x,y)\leqslant 2A\sqrt{\ln(|\mathcal{Y}|)T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\pi,x:\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}A_{t}(x,y)\leqslant 2A\sqrt{\ln(|\mathcal{Y}|)T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of <math id="A7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x,y)=\frac{1}{\eta}\ln\frac{\pi_{t+1}(y|x)}{\pi_{t}(y|x)}-r(x,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x,y)=\frac{1}{\eta}\ln\frac{\pi_{t+1}(y|x)}{\pi_{t}(y|x)}-r(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A7.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>exp</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp</annotation></semantics></math> on both sides, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall x,y:\quad\pi_{t+1}(y|x)=\pi_{t}(y|x)\exp\left(\eta\left(r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)\right)\right)=\frac{\pi_{t}(y|x)\exp\left(\eta(r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x))\right)}{\exp(-\eta\Delta_{\mu}(x))}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall x,y:\quad\pi_{t+1}(y|x)=\pi_{t}(y|x)\exp\left(\eta\left(r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)\right)\right)=\frac{\pi_{t}(y|x)\exp\left(\eta(r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x))\right)}{\exp(-\eta\Delta_{\mu}(x))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(x,y):=r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(x,y):=r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">and the advantage</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{t}(x,y)=g_{t}(x,y)-\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}g_{t}(x,y^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}(x,y)=g_{t}(x,y)-\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}g_{t}(x,y^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">We can rewrite the above update rule as:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x,y:\quad\pi_{t+1}(y|x)\propto\pi_{t}(y|x)\exp\left(\eta A_{t}(x,y)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x,y:\quad\pi_{t+1}(y|x)\propto\pi_{t}(y|x)\exp\left(\eta A_{t}(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The remain part of the proof is similar to the analysis of NPG in <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix F Proof of Chapter ‣ On the Sample Complexity of Differentially Private Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ Appendix D Differentially Private REBEL ‣ On the Sample Complexity of Differentially Private Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We know that:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}r(x,y)-\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}r(x,y)\right)=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}r(x,y)-\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}r(x,y)\right)=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A_{t}(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A_{t}(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leqslant}2A\sqrt{\frac{\ln(|\mathcal{Y}|)}{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leqslant}2A\sqrt{\frac{\ln(|\mathcal{Y}|)}{T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y)\right)^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y)\right)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) holds by  Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma12" title="Lemma 12. ‣ Appendix G Proof of Appendix ‣ On the Sample Complexity of Differentially Private Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then we need to bound: <math id="A7.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of concentrability coefficient <math id="A7.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex142.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now bound <math id="A7.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(r(x,y)-\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y)+\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}g_{t}(x,y^{\prime}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(r(x,y)-\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y)+\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}g_{t}(x,y^{\prime}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant 2\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y)-g_{t}(x,y)\right)^{2}+2\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant 2\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y)-g_{t}(x,y)\right)^{2}+2\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the <math id="A7.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(x,y)=r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(x,y)=r(x,y)+\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma11" title="Lemma 11. ‣ Appendix G Proof of Appendix ‣ On the Sample Complexity of Differentially Private Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, we can see that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(r(x,y)-g_{t}(x,y))^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x))^{2}\leqslant\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⩽</mo><msubsup><mi>err</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(r(x,y)-g_{t}(x,y))^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}(\Delta(x,y)-\Delta_{\mu}(x))^{2}\leqslant\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(r(x,y^{\prime})-g_{t}(x,y^{\prime})\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex147.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(\Delta(x,y^{\prime})-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(\Delta(x,y^{\prime})-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(\Delta(x,y^{\prime})-\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)+\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(\Delta(x,y^{\prime})-\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)+\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant 2\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(\Delta(x,y^{\prime})-\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)\right)^{2}+2\mathbb{E}_{x}\left(\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant 2\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)}\left(\Delta(x,y^{\prime})-\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)\right)^{2}+2\mathbb{E}_{x}\left(\Delta_{\pi_{t}}(x)-\Delta_{\mu}(x)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant 4\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant 4\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality uses Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma11" title="Lemma 11. ‣ Appendix G Proof of Appendix ‣ On the Sample Complexity of Differentially Private Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> again.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining things together, we can conclude that:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}\leqslant C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}(10\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><msubsup><mi>err</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)-A_{t}(x,y))^{2}\leqslant C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}(10\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we can derive our main theorem:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{x,y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left(A^{\pi_{t}}(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant 2A\sqrt{\frac{\ln|\mathcal{Y}|}{T}}+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t}\sqrt{10C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>err</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant 2A\sqrt{\frac{\ln|\mathcal{Y}|}{T}}+\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t}\sqrt{10C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}\mathrm{err}^{2}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2A\sqrt{\frac{\ln|\mathcal{Y}|}{T}}+\frac{\sqrt{10C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}}}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathrm{err}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>err</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2A\sqrt{\frac{\ln|\mathcal{Y}|}{T}}+\frac{\sqrt{10C_{\mu\to\pi^{*}}}}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathrm{err}_{t}(m,\varepsilon,\delta,\zeta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Environment.</span> We conduct experiments on the <span id="A8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CartPole-v1</span> environment from OpenAI Gym, a standard benchmark for evaluating policy gradient methods. The task requires balancing a pole on a moving cart, with a maximum episode reward of 500.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Policy Parameterization.</span> Policies are represented by two-layer fully-connected neural networks with 64 hidden units, ReLU activation, and softmax output layer, i.e., the architecture is <math id="A8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Linear}(4,64)\to\text{ReLU}\to\text{Linear}(64,2)\to\text{Softmax}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>Softmax</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Linear}(4,64)\to\text{ReLU}\to\text{Linear}(64,2)\to\text{Softmax}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Privacy Settings.</span> We evaluate privacy-preserving algorithms under two privacy budgets: <math id="A8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,\delta)=(5,10^{-5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,\delta)=(5,10^{-5})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,\delta)=(3,10^{-5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,\delta)=(3,10^{-5})</annotation></semantics></math>, representing moderate and strong privacy guarantees respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Details.</span> All algorithms are trained for 100 epochs with batch size 10 (i.e., 10 episodes per gradient update) and discount factor <math id="A8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>. We use advantage normalization with baseline subtraction for variance reduction. Each algorithm is trained with 3 random seeds, and we report the average performance with standard deviation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation.</span> We evaluate performance using three metrics: (i) <span id="A8.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mean Final Reward</span>: average reward in the final epoch across all seeds, (ii) <span id="A8.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Std Final Reward</span>: standard deviation of final rewards across seeds, and (iii) <span id="A8.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best Epoch Mean</span>: highest average reward achieved during training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results.</span> Table <a href="#A8.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ On the Sample Complexity of Differentially Private Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the performance under different privacy settings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A8.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
